(function () {
  window.DENO_DOC_SEARCH_INDEX = {"kind":"search","nodes":[{"id":"namespace_createclient","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"createClient","file":"client.ts","doc":"Creates an RTSP client on a connection that is already open.Each request gets the next CSeq, starting at 1, in place of any CSeq the caller set. A response resolves the request with the same CSeq, whatever case the server writes that name in, so responses may arrive in any order. A 1xx response is interim and is skipped: the request keeps waiting for the final one. A response whose CSeq matches no waiting request is ignored.The connection ends on close(), when the server ends it, or when its readable or writable side fails. Every waiting request then rejects and every later one rejects at once, as request describes.","url":"./client.ts/~/createClient.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_client","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"Client","file":"client.ts","doc":"An RTSP client, made by createClient.","url":"./client.ts/~/Client.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_client","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Client.request","file":"client.ts","doc":"Sends a request and resolves with its final response.The other header fields go out in the order and the spelling given. The client sets CSeq itself, on a copy: the request passed in and its headers are left as they are. A CSeq the caller did set, in any case, keeps its place and its spelling and gets the client's number, and later ones are left out. Without one, CSeq goes last.Rejects when the connection ends before the response arrives, and at once when it has ended already: with an Error whose message is RTSP client is closed after close(), with one whose message is RTSP connection ended after the server ended the connection, and with the error of the readable or writable side, as it is, after that side failed.","url":"./client.ts/~/Client.request.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_client","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Client.channel","file":"client.ts","doc":"Claims a Channel ID (0 to 255) and returns its two sides.The readable side gives the binary data of each $ block the server sends on this Channel ID, in order. The writable side sends each chunk written as one $ block, so a chunk holds at most 65535 octets. Closing or aborting the writable side leaves the connection open.Calling it again for a claimed Channel ID returns the same pair. Cancelling the readable side gives the Channel ID up: $ blocks for it are dropped and counted again, and the next call returns a fresh pair that starts with the blocks that arrive after it. Nothing is replayed.A claimed channel has to be read. The client handles what the server sends in order, so one unread $ block holds back everything behind it, responses included, until the block is read or the readable side is cancelled.close() closes the readable side. A connection that fails or is ended by the server fails it with the error that request() rejects with. From then on, writing rejects with that error, and a call for a Channel ID claims nothing: it returns a pair whose readable side has failed with it.","url":"./client.ts/~/Client.channel.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_client","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Client.droppedBlocks","file":"client.ts","doc":"How many $ blocks were dropped, by Channel ID, because nobody had claimed that Channel ID when they arrived. A live view: it changes as blocks are dropped.","url":"./client.ts/~/Client.droppedBlocks.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_client","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Client.close","file":"client.ts","doc":"Ends the connection: closes the writable side once everything written has gone out, cancels the readable side, rejects the requests still waiting and closes the readable side of every claimed channel.Resolves when both sides are done, so it waits for a server that is slow to take what was written. Rejects with the error of the writable side when closing it fails. Calling it again, or after the connection has ended some other way, does nothing.","url":"./client.ts/~/Client.close.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clientoptions","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"ClientOptions","file":"client.ts","doc":"The two sides of the connection a client runs on, and how it answers the server.","url":"./client.ts/~/ClientOptions.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clientoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ClientOptions.readable","file":"client.ts","doc":"The octets the server sends.","url":"./client.ts/~/ClientOptions.readable.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clientoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ClientOptions.writable","file":"client.ts","doc":"Where the octets for the server go.","url":"./client.ts/~/ClientOptions.writable.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clientoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ClientOptions.onRequest","file":"client.ts","doc":"Answers a request sent by the server. Default: 501 Not Implemented.The client sets the request's CSeq on a copy of the answer, so the handler does not have to. A CSeq the handler did set, in any case, keeps its place and its spelling and gets the request's value. Without one, CSeq goes last, spelled the way the server spelled it. The handler does not hold the connection up: responses and $ blocks that arrive while it works are handled, and answers go out in the order the handlers finish.When the handler throws or rejects, the server gets 500 Internal Server Error and the error is reported nowhere else, so a handler that wants its errors seen catches them itself.","url":"./client.ts/~/ClientOptions.onRequest.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_decodeinterleavedbinarydata","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"decodeInterleavedBinaryData","file":"encoding/interleaved.ts","doc":"Decodes one $ block from the start of octets.Short input is normal on a stream, so it is not an error: the result is undefined until the whole block has arrived. Octets after the block are left alone, bytesRead says where the next item starts.The returned binaryData is a copy. It stays valid after the caller reuses or overwrites the buffer behind octets.The caller checks that the first octet is $ before calling. It is not checked here.","url":"./encoding/interleaved.ts/~/decodeInterleavedBinaryData.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_encodeinterleavedbinarydata","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"encodeInterleavedBinaryData","file":"encoding/interleaved.ts","doc":"Encodes one $ block.The caller keeps channelId within 0-255 and binaryData within 65535 octets. Larger values do not fit their fields and wrap silently.","url":"./encoding/interleaved.ts/~/encodeInterleavedBinaryData.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_isinterleavedbinarydata","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"isInterleavedBinaryData","file":"encoding/interleaved.ts","doc":"Tells a $ block apart from an RTSP message in what the decode stream emits.","url":"./encoding/interleaved.ts/~/isInterleavedBinaryData.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_interleavedbinarydata","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"InterleavedBinaryData","file":"encoding/interleaved.ts","doc":"One $ block: the channel it travels on and the upper-layer PDU it carries.","url":"./encoding/interleaved.ts/~/InterleavedBinaryData.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_interleavedbinarydata","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"InterleavedBinaryData.channelId","file":"encoding/interleaved.ts","doc":"Channel ID, 0-255, as agreed in the Transport header's interleaved.","url":"./encoding/interleaved.ts/~/InterleavedBinaryData.channelId.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_interleavedbinarydata","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"InterleavedBinaryData.binaryData","file":"encoding/interleaved.ts","doc":"One upper-layer PDU, at most 65535 octets.","url":"./encoding/interleaved.ts/~/InterleavedBinaryData.binaryData.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_decodemessage","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"decodeMessage","file":"encoding/message.ts","doc":"Decodes one RTSP message from the front of octets.Empty lines before the start-line are skipped and counted in the bytes read. The header section ends at the first empty line. The body is as many octets as the first Content-Length says, whatever its case, and none without that header.Each header line becomes one pair, in the order of the lines. The name is everything before the first colon, in the case it was written in, without the spaces or tabs between it and the colon. The value is the rest, without the whitespace around it. A folded value (CRLF followed by spaces or tabs) is unfolded to one space. Lines with the same name stay separate pairs.The start-line and the header fields are read one character per octet, so an octet above 127 comes out as the character with that code.The returned messageBody is a copy, so the caller may reuse octets.","url":"./encoding/message.ts/~/decodeMessage.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_encodemessage","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"encodeMessage","file":"encoding/message.ts","doc":"Encodes one RTSP message.Each pair of headerFields is written as one line, in the order given and with the name as given.When messageBody is not empty, Content-Length is set to its length. If headerFields holds that name already, in any case, the first such pair keeps its place and its spelling and gets the new value, and later pairs with that name are left out. Otherwise Content-Length is written as the last line. The frame's headerFields and its pairs are not changed.The start-line and the header fields are written one octet per character, so every character in them must have a code below 256.","url":"./encoding/message.ts/~/encodeMessage.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_headerfield","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"HeaderField","file":"encoding/message.ts","doc":"One header field: its name exactly as written, and its value.","url":"./encoding/message.ts/~/HeaderField.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_messageframe","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"MessageFrame","file":"encoding/message.ts","doc":"One RTSP message split into its three parts, with the start-line still a plain string.","url":"./encoding/message.ts/~/MessageFrame.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_messageframe","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"MessageFrame.startLine","file":"encoding/message.ts","doc":"The Request-Line or Status-Line, without its CRLF.","url":"./encoding/message.ts/~/MessageFrame.startLine.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_messageframe","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"MessageFrame.headerFields","file":"encoding/message.ts","doc":"The header fields, one pair per line, in the order of the lines. A name that is on several lines is in several pairs. Folded values are already unfolded.","url":"./encoding/message.ts/~/MessageFrame.headerFields.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_messageframe","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"MessageFrame.messageBody","file":"encoding/message.ts","doc":"The message body, empty when the message has none.","url":"./encoding/message.ts/~/MessageFrame.messageBody.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_isrequest","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"isRequest","file":"protocol/message.ts","doc":"Checks whether a value is a request, by its method field.","url":"./protocol/message.ts/~/isRequest.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_isresponse","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"isResponse","file":"protocol/message.ts","doc":"Checks whether a value is a response, by its statusCode field.","url":"./protocol/message.ts/~/isResponse.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_parsemessage","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"parseMessage","file":"protocol/message.ts","doc":"Reads a frame as a request or a response.A start-line that begins with RTSP/ is a Status-Line, so the frame is a response. Any other start-line is a Request-Line.","url":"./protocol/message.ts/~/parseMessage.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_serializemessage","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"serializeMessage","file":"protocol/message.ts","doc":"Writes a request or a response as a frame, ready for encodeMessage.","url":"./protocol/message.ts/~/serializeMessage.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtspmessage","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"RtspMessage","file":"protocol/message.ts","doc":"An RTSP message: a request or a response.","url":"./protocol/message.ts/~/RtspMessage.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_parserequest","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"parseRequest","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"Reads a frame whose start-line is a Request-Line: Method SP Request-URI SP RTSP-Version.The header fields and the message body are passed on as they are, not copied.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/parseRequest.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_serializerequest","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"serializeRequest","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"Writes a request as a frame, ready for encodeMessage.The header fields and the message body are passed on as they are, not copied.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/serializeRequest.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtsprequest","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"RtspRequest","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"An RTSP request.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/RtspRequest.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtsprequest","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspRequest.method","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"The method, such as \"DESCRIBE\", kept as written.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/RtspRequest.method.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtsprequest","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspRequest.requestUri","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"\"*\" or an RTSP URI.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/RtspRequest.requestUri.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtsprequest","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspRequest.rtspVersion","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"The version, such as \"RTSP/2.0\" or \"RTSP/1.0\", kept as written.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/RtspRequest.rtspVersion.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtsprequest","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspRequest.headers","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"The header fields, one pair per line, in the order of the lines and with each name as written. new Headers(request.headers) looks a name up whatever its case.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/RtspRequest.headers.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtsprequest","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspRequest.messageBody","file":"protocol/request.ts","doc":"The message body, empty when there is none.","url":"./protocol/request.ts/~/RtspRequest.messageBody.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_parseresponse","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"parseResponse","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"Reads a frame whose start-line is a Status-Line: RTSP-Version SP Status-Code SP Reason-Phrase.Everything after the second space is the Reason-Phrase, spaces included. The header fields and the message body are passed on as they are, not copied.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/parseResponse.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_serializeresponse","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"serializeResponse","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"Writes a response as a frame, ready for encodeMessage.The space after the Status-Code is always written, also in front of an empty Reason-Phrase. The header fields and the message body are passed on as they are, not copied.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/serializeResponse.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtspresponse","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"RtspResponse","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"An RTSP response.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/RtspResponse.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtspresponse","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspResponse.rtspVersion","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"The version, such as \"RTSP/2.0\" or \"RTSP/1.0\", kept as written.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/RtspResponse.rtspVersion.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtspresponse","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspResponse.statusCode","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"The Status-Code, such as 200. A 1xx code is an interim response.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/RtspResponse.statusCode.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtspresponse","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspResponse.reasonPhrase","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"The text after the Status-Code. It may hold spaces and may be empty.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/RtspResponse.reasonPhrase.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtspresponse","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspResponse.headers","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"The header fields, one pair per line, in the order of the lines and with each name as written. new Headers(response.headers) looks a name up whatever its case.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/RtspResponse.headers.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_rtspresponse","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"RtspResponse.messageBody","file":"protocol/response.ts","doc":"The message body, empty when there is none.","url":"./protocol/response.ts/~/RtspResponse.messageBody.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_creatertspdecodestream","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"createRtspDecodeStream","file":"streams/decode.ts","doc":"Creates a stream that turns the octets of an RTSP connection into RTSP messages and interleaved binary data, in the order they arrive.Empty lines (CRLF) between items are skipped. After them, a $ starts interleaved binary data and any other octet starts a message. An item that is not all there yet is kept until the next chunk, and a chunk that holds several items emits all of them.Emitted items do not share memory with the chunks written, so the writer may reuse its buffer.When the stream ends inside an item, the readable side fails with an Error whose message is RTSP stream ended inside an item with N octets left over. Ending between items, or after empty lines only, is a clean end.","url":"./streams/decode.ts/~/createRtspDecodeStream.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_creatertspencodestream","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"createRtspEncodeStream","file":"streams/encode.ts","doc":"Creates a stream that turns RTSP messages and interleaved binary data into the octets of an RTSP connection.Each item written comes out as one chunk, so an item is never split and two items never mix. A message with a message body gets its Content-Length set, as encodeMessage does.","url":"./streams/encode.ts/~/createRtspEncodeStream.html","deprecated":false}]};
})()